diff --git a/NOTES.md b/NOTES.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..d36b32d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/NOTES.md
@@ -0,0 +1,84 @@
+# Credit control – implementation notes
+
+**Status: partial.** I delivered the review / stop / watch / enforcement / report slice of `task/brd.md`
+(BR-01 to BR-11, BR-30, BR-32 partly, BR-33/34, BR-39 to BR-43 partly). I did **not** build dunning letters, interest and
+fees, bad-debt write-off, the month-end ledger reconciliation, or the portal reminder/charge views
+(BR-12 to BR-29, BR-31, BR-35, BR-37, BR-38). Nothing here was run: there was no PHP or database available, so
+all of it is untested code. Please review and run it on a copy of the database before relying on it.
+
+## Design choice: reuse what webERP already has
+
+webERP already has credit status codes (`holdreasons`, `debtorsmaster.holdreason`) where `dissallowinvoices` is
+1 = block and 2 = watch, and the order-entry pages already read them. So:
+- **Stop** = a customer whose status code has `dissallowinvoices = 1`; **watch** = `2`; **normal** = `0`.
+- Update 44 adds two codes: 99 "Credit stop" and 98 "Credit watch" (config `CreditStopReasonCode`, `CreditWatchReasonCode`).
+  Existing codes keep working.
+
+## What changed
+
+**Schema (existing systems and new installs)**
+- `sql/updates/44.php` (picked up automatically by the upgrade screen): tables `creditreviews`, `creditcontrollog`;
+  `debtorsmaster.nextreviewdate`; `salesorders.creditheld` (0 none, 1 held over limit, 2 released); hold codes 98/99;
+  config `CreditReviewMonths` (12), `CreditStopReasonCode`, `CreditWatchReasonCode`; security token 21 "Credit control"
+  (granted to role 8, system administrator); scripts and AR menu items.
+- Existing customers get `nextreviewdate = today + CreditReviewMonths` (BR-40). Existing status and stop codes are untouched.
+- New installs: `install/sql/tables/{creditreviews,creditcontrollog,debtorsmaster,salesorders}.sql`;
+  `install/sql/data/{holdreasons,creditcontrol_config,creditcontrol_scripts,creditcontrol_menuitems,securitytokens,securitygroups}.sql`;
+  and the demo data tail of `install/sql/demo.sql`. The installer sets `DBUpdateNumber` to the highest update file,
+  so the install SQL has to carry everything update 44 does. It does.
+
+**New code**
+- `includes/CreditControlFunctions.php`: status lookup, insert-only audit log, `SetCreditStatus`, over-limit hold,
+  dispatch/invoice block check.
+- `CreditReview.php` (token 21): record a review (outcome, new limit, notes, next review date) – limit, review and
+  log are written in one transaction (BR-01, 03, 04, 05); stop/watch/off with reason; full history per customer (BR-32).
+- `CreditHeldOrders.php` (token 21): release held orders / orders for customers on stop with a reason; list of orders
+  taken for customers on watch (BR-06, 08, 10).
+- `CreditControlReport.php` (token 2): due/overdue reviews, over limit (and by how much), watch/stop; filter by rep and
+  currency; home-currency totals. A user with a `SalesmanLogin` is forced to their own customers (BR-30, 33).
+
+**Enforcement of stop, by route** (BR-06)
+- Sales office and web shop: `DeliveryDetails.php` refuses to save a new order (also quotation→order) for a stopped customer.
+  `SelectOrderItems.php`: portal customers on stop get a "contact us" message (BR-11); customers on watch can now order
+  (before, any non-zero code blocked them, which contradicted BR-08).
+- Counter sales (`CounterSales.php`), special orders (`SpecialOrder.php`), EDI (`EDIProcessOrders.php`),
+  standing orders (`RecurringSalesOrdersProcess.php`, template left untouched so it recurs after the stop is lifted),
+  API order creation and invoicing (`api/includes/api_salesorders.php`, new error code `CustomerOnStop` = 9001).
+- Dispatch/invoice of existing orders: `ConfirmDispatch_Invoice.php` (every request, including the posting one)
+  and the API `InvoiceSalesOrder` refuse unless the order was released.
+- Over-limit orders: after save, an order that puts the customer over the limit is flagged `creditheld=1` and cannot be
+  invoiced until released (BR-10). Applies in order entry, EDI and standing orders (which also skip auto-invoice).
+
+**Permissions** (BR-07, 34): credit limit and status are removed from `Customers.php`'s UPDATE, so no one can change them
+there; the fields are read-only. New customers get status "no hold", the default limit and a next review date. Changes go
+through `CreditReview.php`, which needs token 21. Also: `Z_ImportDebtors.php`, `api_customers.php` and
+`Z_ChangeCustomerCode.php` set/carry `nextreviewdate`; the latter moves the history rows with the customer code.
+
+**Display** (BR-09): `CustomerAccount.php` / `CustomerInquiry.php` show "ON WATCH" (not shown to portal logins, per
+open question 10) or "ON HOLD".
+
+**Docs** (BR-42, 43): new "Credit Control" section and sales-staff note in `doc/Manual/ManualAccountsReceivable.html`.
+
+## Not done / known gaps
+- Dunning, interest/fees, waivers, write-offs, approval threshold, GL postings, disputed invoices, aged-debt columns (BR-31),
+  portal views, ledger reconciliation (BR-12 to BR-29, 31, 35, 37, 38). These need GL posting design that I could not test.
+- The API `ModifyCustomer` still accepts `holdreason`/`creditlimit` from any authenticated API user.
+- Portal pages still print the status description text ("Credit watch") in the account header.
+- AC-12 (staff guide signed off by Maria and the Sales Manager) is a business step.
+- Credit-control user roles: only role 8 gets token 21 automatically. Finance must grant it to the credit controller,
+  deputy and Finance Director roles. Nobody else should hold it.
+- "Watch" warning at order entry already existed only at customer selection; I did not add more warnings.
+
+## Ambiguities and how I resolved them
+- **Existing hold codes with `dissallowinvoices = -1`** (the demo data and column default): other screens show them as
+  "on hold" but order entry never blocked them. I kept that: only `1` is a stop (BR-41, no behaviour change for existing data).
+- **Over-limit hold vs the existing `CheckCreditLimits` option** (0 off, 1 warn, 2 refuse): I hold orders when the option is
+  1 or 2, and leave it off when Finance has turned the check off. At 2 the old refusal still applies first. Open question 5
+  (web shop/standing: hold or reject) – I chose hold everywhere.
+- **Limit "over" test**: for the held-order check I use credit available including open orders (existing
+  `GetCreditAvailable`); the report uses balance > limit.
+- **Edited orders**: an edit re-assesses the order, so a release does not survive changes. Orders taken before a stop can still be edited.
+- **Who changes limits/status**: a single new token (21) rather than a "deputy" concept; roles are assigned by the administrator.
+- **Rep ownership** is "any branch of the customer assigned to the rep" in the report; existing pages keep their own rules.
+- **Review period** is one global value, not per risk band (BR-02 "shorter for higher-risk"): rep sets the date on each review.
+- **Open questions 1–12** are unanswered by the BRD; I only touched 5, 8 (reps see status and reason description), 10 (watch hidden from portal).
