     <a class="minitext" href="#top">⬆ Top</a>
 </div>
 
+<h2><a id="CreditControl">Credit Control</a></h2>
+
+<p>Only credit control staff (the credit controller, the deputy and the Finance Director - users holding security token 21, "Credit control") can change credit limits or put customers on or off stop or watch. Sales reps and the sales office can see the status but cannot change it.</p>
+
+<h3>Credit reviews</h3>
+<p>Accounts Receivable &gt; Credit Reviews, Stop and Watch. Find the customer (tick "only customers due or overdue for review" to list the work due), choose the outcome (limit confirmed, raised, reduced, put on watch, put on stop, or take off watch/stop), enter the new limit if the limit changes, the notes (required) and the next review date. The limit changes together with the review that explains it. Reviews and the credit control history cannot be changed or deleted. The standard review period is the configuration value <code>CreditReviewMonths</code> (12 by default). The credit status codes used for stop and watch are the configuration values <code>CreditStopReasonCode</code> (99) and <code>CreditWatchReasonCode</code> (98).</p>
+
+<h3>Stop and watch</h3>
+<p>While a customer is on stop, no new order can be accepted for them in order entry, the web shop, counter sales, special orders, EDI, standing (recurring) orders or the API. Orders taken before the stop cannot be dispatched or invoiced unless credit control releases them (Accounts Receivable &gt; Orders Held for Credit Control). A customer on watch can still be supplied; whoever takes the order is warned, and credit control sees the orders on the same page.</p>
+
+<h3>Over-limit orders</h3>
+<p>When the system option to check credit limits is on, an order that takes the customer over their credit limit (counting open orders) is accepted but held; it cannot be dispatched or invoiced until credit control releases it. Editing a held or released order assesses it again.</p>
+
+<h3>Credit control report</h3>
+<p>Accounts Receivable &gt; Credit Control Report lists customers due or overdue for review, customers over their credit limit, and customers on watch or stop, filtered by sales rep and currency, with totals in the home currency. A sales rep only sees their own customers.</p>
+
+<h3>Note for sales staff</h3>
+<p><b>Watch</b> means you can take orders but you will see a warning and credit control will see the order - talk to the customer about their account. <b>Stop</b> means the system will not accept the order; do not promise delivery, and refer the customer to credit control.</p>
+
 <h2><a id="CustomerNotes">Customer Notes</a></h2>
 
 <p>Customer notes containing any text - a web-link if required and a date can be entered from the Select Customer screen - for the selected customer. The notes are displayed in sequence of priority - so pressing issues appear at the top of the list. These notes might contain information about recent contact with the customer or disputes. There is no checking on the content of the notes and no limit to either the number of notes nor the number of characters that can be used.</p>
diff --git a/includes/CreditControlFunctions.php b/includes/CreditControlFunctions.php
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..8d6d5ec
--- /dev/null
+++ b/includes/CreditControlFunctions.php
@@ -0,0 +1,163 @@
+<?php
+
+/* Shared credit control functions: credit status (normal / watch / stop), the credit control audit log and
+ * the over-limit order hold. Credit status is held in debtorsmaster.holdreason, which points at holdreasons;
+ * holdreasons.dissallowinvoices is 1 for a stop and 2 for a watch (as already used by the order entry pages).
+ */
+
+define('CREDIT_NORMAL', 'normal');
+define('CREDIT_WATCH', 'watch');
+define('CREDIT_STOP', 'stop');
+
+/* Security token that identifies credit control staff (credit controller, deputy, finance director) */
+define('CREDIT_CONTROL_TOKEN', 21);
+
+function CanChangeCreditControl() {
+	return isset($_SESSION['AllowedPageSecurityTokens'])
+		and is_array($_SESSION['AllowedPageSecurityTokens'])
+		and in_array(CREDIT_CONTROL_TOKEN, $_SESSION['AllowedPageSecurityTokens']);
+}
+
+/* Returns array('status' => normal|watch|stop, 'reasoncode', 'reasondescription') or false if no such customer */
+function GetCreditStatus($DebtorNo) {
+	$SQL = "SELECT debtorsmaster.holdreason,
+					holdreasons.reasondescription,
+					holdreasons.dissallowinvoices
+			FROM debtorsmaster
+			INNER JOIN holdreasons
+				ON debtorsmaster.holdreason = holdreasons.reasoncode
+			WHERE debtorsmaster.debtorno = '" . DB_escape_string($DebtorNo) . "'";
+	$Result = DB_query($SQL);
+	if (DB_num_rows($Result) == 0) {
+		return false;
+	}
+	$MyRow = DB_fetch_array($Result);
+	if ($MyRow['dissallowinvoices'] == 1) {
+		$Status = CREDIT_STOP;
+	} elseif ($MyRow['dissallowinvoices'] == 2) {
+		$Status = CREDIT_WATCH;
+	} else {
+		$Status = CREDIT_NORMAL;
+	}
+	return array('status' => $Status,
+				'reasoncode' => $MyRow['holdreason'],
+				'reasondescription' => $MyRow['reasondescription']);
+}
+
+function CreditStatusLabel($Status) {
+	switch ($Status) {
+		case CREDIT_STOP:
+			return __('ON STOP');
+		case CREDIT_WATCH:
+			return __('On watch');
+		default:
+			return __('Normal');
+	}
+}
+
+function CustomerIsOnStop($DebtorNo) {
+	$Status = GetCreditStatus($DebtorNo);
+	return ($Status !== false and $Status['status'] == CREDIT_STOP);
+}
+
+/* The standard review period set by Finance (config CreditReviewMonths, default 12) */
+function DefaultNextReviewDate() {
+	$Months = 12;
+	if (isset($_SESSION['CreditReviewMonths']) and is_numeric($_SESSION['CreditReviewMonths']) and $_SESSION['CreditReviewMonths'] > 0) {
+		$Months = (int) $_SESSION['CreditReviewMonths'];
+	}
+	return date('Y-m-d', strtotime('+' . $Months . ' months'));
+}
+
+function GetCreditReasonCode($Status) {
+	if ($Status == CREDIT_STOP) {
+		return isset($_SESSION['CreditStopReasonCode']) ? (int) $_SESSION['CreditStopReasonCode'] : 99;
+	} elseif ($Status == CREDIT_WATCH) {
+		return isset($_SESSION['CreditWatchReasonCode']) ? (int) $_SESSION['CreditWatchReasonCode'] : 98;
+	}
+	return 0;
+}
+
+/* Append to the per customer credit control history. The log is never updated or deleted by the application. */
+function LogCreditEvent($DebtorNo, $EventType, $OldValue, $NewValue, $Reason) {
+	$UserID = isset($_SESSION['UserID']) ? $_SESSION['UserID'] : 'system';
+	$SQL = "INSERT INTO creditcontrollog (debtorno,
+										eventdate,
+										userid,
+										eventtype,
+										oldvalue,
+										newvalue,
+										reason)
+									VALUES (
+										'" . DB_escape_string($DebtorNo) . "',
+										CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,
+										'" . DB_escape_string($UserID) . "',
+										'" . DB_escape_string($EventType) . "',
+										'" . DB_escape_string(mb_substr($OldValue, 0, 100)) . "',
+										'" . DB_escape_string(mb_substr($NewValue, 0, 100)) . "',
+										'" . DB_escape_string($Reason) . "')";
+	DB_query($SQL, __('The credit control log entry could not be saved because'));
+}
+
+/* Sets the credit status of a customer (normal, watch or stop) and logs it. The caller must have checked
+ * CanChangeCreditControl() and be inside a transaction if it matters. Returns false if nothing changed. */
+function SetCreditStatus($DebtorNo, $NewStatus, $Reason) {
+	$Current = GetCreditStatus($DebtorNo);
+	if ($Current === false) {
+		return false;
+	}
+	$NewCode = GetCreditReasonCode($NewStatus);
+	if ($NewStatus != CREDIT_NORMAL) {
+		$CheckResult = DB_query("SELECT reasoncode FROM holdreasons WHERE reasoncode='" . $NewCode . "'");
+		if (DB_num_rows($CheckResult) == 0) {
+			return false;
+		}
+	}
+	if ($Current['status'] == $NewStatus and $Current['reasoncode'] == $NewCode) {
+		return false;
+	}
+	DB_query("UPDATE debtorsmaster SET holdreason='" . $NewCode . "' WHERE debtorno='" . DB_escape_string($DebtorNo) . "'",
+			__('The credit status of the customer could not be updated because'));
+	LogCreditEvent($DebtorNo, 'status', $Current['status'], $NewStatus, $Reason);
+	return true;
+}
+
+/* An order is held for credit control when it takes the customer over their limit (debtorsmaster.creditlimit,
+ * counting open orders - see GetCreditAvailable). Applies when the system wide check on credit limits is on.
+ * Call after the order has been written. Returns true if the order was held. */
+function HoldOrderIfOverCreditLimit($OrderNo, $DebtorNo) {
+	if (!isset($_SESSION['CheckCreditLimits']) or $_SESSION['CheckCreditLimits'] == 0) {
+		return false;
+	}
+	$Result = DB_query("SELECT quotation, creditheld FROM salesorders WHERE orderno='" . (int) $OrderNo . "'");
+	$Order = DB_fetch_array($Result);
+	if (!$Order or $Order['quotation'] != 0) {
+		return false;
+	}
+	/* an edited order is assessed again, so a release does not survive changes to the order */
+	if (GetCreditAvailable($DebtorNo) < 0) {
+		DB_query("UPDATE salesorders SET creditheld=1 WHERE orderno='" . (int) $OrderNo . "'");
+		LogCreditEvent($DebtorNo, 'order held', '', (string) $OrderNo, __('Order takes the customer over their credit limit'));
+		return true;
+	}
+	DB_query("UPDATE salesorders SET creditheld=0 WHERE orderno='" . (int) $OrderNo . "'");
+	return false;
+}
+
+/* Whether goods may be dispatched or invoiced on an existing order. Orders taken before a stop are blocked
+ * unless credit control released them (creditheld = 2). Orders held for the credit limit are blocked until released.
+ * Returns an error message, or '' if the order may proceed. */
+function OrderCreditBlockMessage($OrderNo) {
+	$Result = DB_query("SELECT debtorno, creditheld FROM salesorders WHERE orderno='" . (int) $OrderNo . "'");
+	$Order = DB_fetch_array($Result);
+	if (!$Order) {
+		return '';
+	}
+	if ($Order['creditheld'] == 1) {
+		return __('Order') . ' ' . $OrderNo . ' ' . __('is held for credit control approval because it takes the customer over their credit limit. It cannot be dispatched or invoiced until credit control releases it.');
+	}
+	if ($Order['creditheld'] != 2 and CustomerIsOnStop($Order['debtorno'])) {
+		return __('Customer') . ' ' . $Order['debtorno'] . ' ' . __('is on stop. Order') . ' ' . $OrderNo . ' ' . __('cannot be dispatched or invoiced unless credit control releases it.');
+	}
+	return '';
+}
